    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="1454" n="1442" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1442"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Walter S.
                            Robertson to General Marshall</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-03">3 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6407. Reurad 1224.<anchor n="32" xml:id="d729-f1"/> A 3-way agreement has been
                    signed for the immediate dispatch of a fact-finding team to investigate and
                    report <pb facs="1455" n="1443" xml:id="pg1443"/> upon the ambush of Marine
                    convoy on the Peiping–Tientsin road, 29 July. Field Team 25 has been selected
                    for this mission. Colonel M. F. Davis former general officer who has had broad
                    experience as chairman Team 7 is designated as U. S. member and team
                    chairman.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
